{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDNdesULxgFsL12uyvS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed it. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the shares add up to 100 and nothing gets lost.\n\n**The cause:** `money.py` used whole-number division (`total // people`) and threw away the remainder.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py:5`): it now keeps the remainder from `divmod(total, people)` and gives one extra grosz each to the first few people until it's used up. Shares always add up to the total and never differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Tests** (`test_money.py`): I added two tests and ran them before the fix to confirm they caught the bug:\n- One checks the exact 1 zł / 3 people case.\n- The other checks many total/people combinations: the shares must add up to the total and differ by at most 1.\n\nAll 5 tests now pass.\n\nThe extra grosze always go to the people listed first. If you'd prefer to hand them out another way, such as at random or by rotating who gets them, tell me and I'll change it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":563,"cache_read_input_tokens":19323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":563},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d190c1e9-47b2-42f8-ad7e-de90752e8ae4","uuid":"6ff31458-33be-4ce8-9e21-f16247061c85","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:15:22.669Z","request_id":"req_011CggDNdSiHvSvJirFUdc4d"}
